# Energy efficiency (mandatory)

If the user referenced `@docs/WHAT_WE_DO.md`, read the full docs bundle (`chinese-listener-docs-bundle.mdc`). Otherwise read `docs/WHAT_WE_DO.md` (governance) and `docs/ENERGY_EFFICIENCY.md` (full practices).

## Must

- **Lifecycle-aware work** — cancel coroutines/flows when UI or feature scope ends; no `GlobalScope`.
- **No polling by default** — prefer events, user refresh, or scheduled batch via deferrable background APIs on Android.
- **Flow discipline** — `distinctUntilChanged` / debounce where appropriate; avoid emitting identical `UiState` in tight loops.
- **Layered side effects** — battery/network/sensor code in **data** or platform adapters, not composables or domain.
- **OLED-friendly UI** — explicit `colorScheme` text colors; prefer dark surfaces where product allows.
- **Honest verification** — if claiming battery improvement, say whether profiler/idle test was run or mark unverified.

## Must not (without explicit approval)

- Foreground services, high-frequency location/BLE, `WAKE_LOCK`, `REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS`
- Timers or `while(true)` loops on main thread or in presentation without backoff
- Duplicate network/cache layers that refetch the same data on every recomposition or rotation

## New dependencies

WorkManager, location, analytics, push, heavy media pipelines — **user approval** + Gradle + manifest/permission review.

## Verification

```text
./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest
./gradlew :app:assembleDebug
```

Add **domain/presentation tests** for schedulers and eligibility policies. Device smoke per `docs/RUN_ON_PHYSICAL_DEVICE.md` when background or permission behavior changes.
